e, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 3% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.9%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.54).","It converts 17% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality is a concern: high accruals (-10.0% of assets).","ROE of 1% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.7x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.4% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.5x net debt to EBITDA ($220.4M of cash against $1.7B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, and interest cover is thin at 1.3x.","The current ratio of 0.86 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 0.2% over 3 years, 9.8% over 5 years and 5.9% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 13%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 6.6% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 21%.","Capex runs only 0.0x depreciation (0.0% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 26, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.9%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (5 sales, net $16.2M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.2% (1.4% in dividends).","It has paid a dividend for 21 consecutive years, raising it 16.5% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 37,100 employees, each generates about $201K of revenue, 0.5x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 5.9% a year.","That works out to $34K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.8M (9x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":